 "result_text": "I changed `src/sqlacodegen/generators.py` so MySQL `DOUBLE(11,2)` should no longer be turned into `Double(11, True)`. I haven't run it against a MySQL `DOUBLE(11,2)` column. The existing test suite passes (94 tests), but I added no test for this case.\n\nThe cause was the Float exception in `get_adapted_type`. It lets a `Float`-family type replace the original even when the two compile differently, because on PostgreSQL `Float` can stand in for both `REAL` and `DOUBLE PRECISION`. It was applied to every dialect. For MySQL `DOUBLE(11,2)`, the generic `Double` it picked took `(11, True)` as `(precision, asdecimal)`. The scale of 2 was lost.\n\nThe exception is now skipped when the original type has a scale. In that case the column keeps its dialect-specific type, so MySQL should render `DOUBLE(11, 2)`.",
